    units: 344,
    text: "In September 2026, two newly built public kindergartens attached to residential communities in Anqing, Anhui Province, officially opened. They added 370 high-quality preschool places and 50 childcare slots, easing a shortage of public kindergarten resources in the area. The projects received a total of 3.5 million yuan in government funding.\n\nThe kindergartens are equipped with teaching aids, play and living facilities, as well as high-definition monitoring systems and smart teaching devices. They provide a quality and safe care and education environment for young children. A local resident said that previously public kindergarten resources in the area were tight and sending a child to school required traveling a long distance. Now there is a public-interest kindergarten at the doorstep, which truly solves the problem of long commutes for enrollment.\n\nThe opening of these kindergartens is part of a broader effort across China to shore up weak links in public services in rural and urban areas. In the first eight months of 2026, national general public budget expenditure reached 18.15 trillion yuan, up 1.2 percent year-on-year. Spending related to investing in people grew relatively fast, with social security and employment expenditure up 6.5 percent and health expenditure up 9.2 percent.\n\nCentral government funding of over 12 billion yuan was allocated this year to provide elderly care service consumption subsidies for moderately and severely disabled seniors nationwide, benefiting nearly 2 million elderly people. In Wuhan, Hubei Province, local authorities raised 540 million yuan for such subsidies. An 86-year-old woman who has been paralyzed in bed after a stroke successfully applied for the subsidy, significantly reducing the cost of home care.\n\nMeanwhile, long-term care insurance, sometimes called the “sixth social insurance,” is being expanded from pilot programs to nationwide coverage. After professional assessment, disabled elderly people can receive reimbursement for 50 to 70 percent of nursing costs, effectively easing the care burden on families. In Hebei Province, the long-term care insurance system was fully implemented in April this year. In Nanhe District of Xingtai City, more than 1,000 disabled elderly people have already received benefits under the program.",
    reference: "2026年9月，安徽省安庆市两所新建的小区配套公办幼儿园正式投用，新增优质学前学位370个、托育托位50个，缓解了当地公办园资源紧张的状况。该项目累计投入财政资金350万元。\n\n园内配齐了教学教具、游乐生活设施，并搭载了高清监控、智能教学一体机等现代化设备，为幼儿提供优质、安全的保教环境。一位当地居民说，以前这一片公办园资源比较紧张，送孩子上学要跑很远的路。现在家门口就有一所普惠性幼儿园，实实在在解决了入园远的难题。\n\n这些幼儿园的投用是中国各地补齐城乡公共服务短板这一更大努力的一部分。2026年前8个月，全国一般公共预算支出达18.15万亿元，同比增长1.2%。投资于人相关支出增长较快，其中社会保障和就业支出增长6.5%，卫生健康支出增长9.2%。\n\n今年中央财政安排超120亿元资金，为全国中度以上失能老人发放养老服务消费补贴，惠及近200万老年群体。在湖北武汉，当地筹集养老服务消费补贴资金5.4亿元。一位86岁的老人因脑梗瘫痪在床，成功申领了养老服务消费补贴，大幅降低了居家照护成本。\n\n与此同时，被称为社保“第六险”的长期护理保险正加速从试点推向全国。失能老人经专业评估后，可享受50%至70%的护理费用报销，有效破解了失能家庭的照护难题。今年4月，河北省全面落地长护险制度。在邢台市南和区，已有千余名失能老人享受到了长护险专项待遇。",
